TEXT -2312 984 Left 3 ;EOFR clocks the next task shift register immediately after an EOF is issued (EN2 rising edge, delayed by task time)\nNext task register must be clocked once EOF has had its effect on capdyn output control (EN2).\nFor this purpose, we delay the EOF signal by 50 ms and pilot the task register with this delayed signal, EOFR.\n \nIf we were to pilot task register directly from EOF:\nEOF would not have time to deactivate EN2, causing problems.
